We are doing a Lab Builder toolchain integration design/implementation run.

Work only in:
/home/administrator/infra-config-portal

Goal:
Stop hand-rolling every vendor operation. Add a toolchain abstraction so the app can use the best available tool for Cisco, iLO/HPE, ESXi, and NetApp.

Research and integrate these tool families where useful:
- Cisco: console direct, ser2net/TCP console, Netmiko, Ansible cisco.ios, pyATS/Genie, NAPALM
- HPE/iLO: Redfish direct, HPE iLOrest, python-ilorest
- ESXi/vSphere: Kickstart, govc/govmomi, vSphere API
- NetApp: netapp-ontap Python client, ONTAP REST, Ansible netapp.ontap
- Firmware: local baseline manifest plus vendor package inventory

Tasks:
1. Create a toolchain design report:
   artifacts/codex-runs/toolchain-integration-design.md

2. Add backend tool availability checks:
   - pyserial
   - netmiko
   - ansible
   - cisco.ios collection
   - govc
   - ilorest
   - netapp-ontap
   - pyATS/Genie if installed
   - NAPALM if installed
   Save:
   artifacts/codex-runs/toolchain-availability-report.md

3. Add Make target:
   make provider-lab-toolchain-check

4. Add UI panel under Build Verification:
   Toolchain Readiness

5. Add Cisco console backend abstraction:
   - local_serial
   - tcp_console / ser2net
   Keep local serial working.
   Add config fields for TCP console.

6. Add Cisco managed-state plan:
   - console bootstrap first
   - Ansible/Netmiko after SSH is enabled

7. Add ESXi managed-state plan:
   - iLO/Kickstart for install
   - govc for post-install validation/deploy

8. Add NetApp managed-state plan:
   - netapp-ontap / REST primary
   - SSH fallback

9. Do not run destructive hardware workflows in this run.
10. Run tests and frontend build.
11. Save final report:
   artifacts/codex-runs/toolchain-integration-final-report.md
